<mujoco model="R1_AIR">
  <!-- Unitree R1 AIR (20-DOF: 12 legs + 4 per arm; no waist, no wrist roll; torso + head are part of the
       pelvis_link). Kinematics, inertia and the Air meshes (meshes/air_*.stl: torso/pelvis, shoulders,
       forearm-with-hand) come from the official unitree_ros robots/r1_air_description/R1_AIR.urdf (BSD-3,
       Unitree); leg / foot / ankle-linkage STLs are byte-identical to the EDU ones and shared.
       Collision / joint-default / actuator conventions follow the EDU R1_C++.xml of this bundle, so both
       variants behave alike in contact: sole = box + 4 spheres, torso/head = boxes (a straight URDF conversion collides
       with the pelvis mesh's convex hull, which spans the whole torso and swallows the upper arms), knee /
       hip-pitch / shoulder / forearm meshes collide as on the EDU. ctrlranges = the Air URDF effort limits (hips / knees /
       shoulder pitch+roll 60, ankles 50, shoulder yaw / elbow 33 N·m; = the bench Air plant R1_AIR.xml), not the EDU
       88 / 139: with the EDU limits the Air ran ~20 % faster than the bench at high speed.
       Loaded by the web app's "r1_air" spec (air_scene.xml) for Air packs. -->
  <compiler angle="radian" meshdir="meshes/" autolimits="true" discardvisual="false"/>

  <default>
